       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Bethany Seeger",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02d2a7d0c250c236c34d9",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "2019-05-31T18:45:17.179-0300"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "So I also did some digging.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "According to the XML Schema : Datatypes specification. Section ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#namespaces"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "3.1 Namespace Considerations",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " defines the namespace URI as ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#built-in-datatypes"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema\",",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " but in Section ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#built-in-datatypes"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "3 Built-in Datatypes",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " they specify that when using the prefix for (in their example) an \"int\" it would appear as \"",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": "\"",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "In Fedora this is coming from Jena. Because we set the created and lastModified datetimes we set them using the Calendar type. This makes Jena see them as ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://jena.apache.org/documentation/javadoc/jena/org/apache/jena/datatypes/xsd/XSDDateTime.html"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "XSDDateTime",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " datatypes. So they get the internally defined namespace.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "We could go to Jena and ask, but I imagine they would point to the XML Schema documents (linked above). So we could go to the W3C and ask...or just add # to the end.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "For reference:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "In the ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-kernel-modeshape/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/modeshape/rdf/impl/mappings/PropertyToTriple.java#L81"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "PropertyToTriple",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " converter we call the ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-kernel-modeshape/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/modeshape/rdf/converters/ValueConverter.java#L84-L109"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "ValueConverter",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": ". Because we pass in strings they are considered default datatypes and fall through to the ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-kernel-modeshape/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/modeshape/rdf/converters/ValueConverter.java#L148-L160"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "stringliteral2node",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " which is able to pull the datatype off but only recognizes \"",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#datetime"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#datetime",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": "\" as specifying a datetime. So you can't do range comparisons unless you use the #.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
