  "description": "<p>Related to: RDF namespaces</p>\n\n<p>There appears to be a potential issue with \"xs: <a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema</a>\" as a predefined namespace binding. It may be missing \"#\" at the end? </p>\n\n<p>When defining a data type for objects of a triple, using the Fedora UI's SPARQL update feature, with the following insert: `&lt;&gt; dc:date \"2019-05-22\"^^xs:dateTime .`</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>The resulting triple (n-triples) is: </p>\n\n<p>&lt;<a href=\"http://annadora.tacc.utexas.edu:8080/fcrepo/rest/2019-03-15-sparql-test\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://annadora.tacc.utexas.edu:8080/fcrepo/rest/2019-03-15-sparql-test</a>&gt; &lt;<a href=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date</a>&gt; \"2019-05-22\"^^&lt;*<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchemadateTime*\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchemadateTime*</a>&gt; .</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>However, all fedora-generated triples with dateTime data types are serialized as:</p>\n\n<p>&lt;<a href=\"http://annadora.tacc.utexas.edu:8080/fcrepo/rest/2019-03-15-sparql-test\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://annadora.tacc.utexas.edu:8080/fcrepo/rest/2019-03-15-sparql-test</a>&gt; &lt;<a href=\"http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#lastModified\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#lastModified</a>&gt; \"2019-05-22T20:07:16.187Z\"^^&lt;*<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime*\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime*</a>&gt; .</p>\n\n<p> </p>",
